<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ImpactsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Impacts on' connection of an Impact Chain model. Indicates mainly a relationship between an impact and an exposed asset. Links an Impact factor to an Exposure factor. Example: An increase in power outages (Impact) impacts industries (Exposure)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#VulnerabilityFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ImpactChainFactor> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#UnderlyingRiskDriverFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "It refers to the (non-climatic) risk drivers that may significantly alter the socio-economic or environmental situations and possibly amplify the negative consequences of impacts by acting on their determinants (e.g., vulnerability or exposure) but cannot be mitigated or controlled within the scope of the Impact Chain model."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#medium> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Medium confidence level. This refers to moderate evidence, which includes news reports, stakeholder input, expert opinions, and combinations of these sources."@en .
