<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#AdaptationFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "IPCC WGII AR5 (https://www.ipcc.ch/site/assets/uploads/2018/02/WGIIAR5-PartA_FINAL.pdf): categories of adaptation options (page 845) (Field et al., 2014)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#RiskFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Risk factor of an Impact Chain model."@en .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b38 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#VulnerabilityFactor> .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b16 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#VulnerabilityFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Vulnerability refers to the predisposition/propensity of exposed elements such as human beings, their livelihoods, and assets to be adversely affected by a natural hazard. This element contributes to and encompasses a variety of concepts and elements, including sensitivity or susceptibility to harm and/or lack of capacity to prevent, prepare, respond, cope and/or adapt (IPCC, 2021)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#minutesToHours> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ConnectionTimeLag> .
