_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b23 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#isAbout> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "\"Definition of FRBROO A Conceptual Model for Bibliographic Information in Object-Oriented Formalism\"\n\nPrepared by: Working Group on FRBR/CRM Dialogue (also referred to as: International Working Group on\nFRBR and CIDOC CRM Harmonisation), affiliated to the IFLA FRBR Review Group, reporting to the IFLA Cataloguing Section\n\nEdited by:\nChryssoula Bekiari, Martin Doerr, Patrick Le Bœuf, Pat Riva\n\nWith contributions from:\nTrond Aalberg, Jérôme Barthélémy, Chryssoula Bekiari, Guillaume Boutard, Martin Doerr, Günther Görz, Dolores Iorizzo, Max Jacob, Carlos Lamsfus, Patrick Le Bœuf, Mika Nyman, João Oliveira, Christian Emil Ore, Allen H. Renear, Pat Riva, Richard Smiraglia, Stephen Stead, Maja Žumer, and others"@en .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b12 .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b40 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#AdaptationFactor> .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b26 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b21 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b22 .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b30 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> _:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b31 .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b25 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ExposureFactor> .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b56 <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#argument1> <urn:swrl:var#z> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#> <http://purl.org/vocommons/voaf#metadataVoc> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#VulnerabilityFactor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#minutesToHours> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "minutes to hours"@en .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b48 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#Affects> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#monthsToYears> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ConfidenceLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Enumeration of confidence values. Applicable to Impact Chain elements such as factors and connections. Evaluated using a qualitative method based on evidence, reflecting the IPCC's approach to evaluating the validity of elements."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#Mitigates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Mitigates' connection of an Impact Chain model. Indicates a relationship that aims to reduce vulnerability or impacts. Links an Adaptation factor to a Vulnerability/Impact factor. Example: An improved irrigation technique (adaptation measure) mitigates the decrease in crop yield (impact) during droughts."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "[ICconnection --source--> ICFactor]: This property is meant to be used to link the reification of an Impact Chain binary connection with its first argument."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#hoursToDays> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ConnectionTimeLag> .
_:n6a5482b0be8542ed98b25705ddbd4321b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ImpactChainFactor> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ExposureFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The (presence of) people, livelihoods, species or ecosystems, environmental functions, services, and resources, infrastructure, or economic, social, or cultural assets in places and settings that could be adversely affected (IPCC, 2021)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#LeadsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Leads to' connection of an Impact Chain model. Indicates a relationship where one factor contributes to another (often indicating a causal relationship). Links a Hazard to a Hazard/Impact factor, or an Impact to another Impact factor. Example: An increase in average temperature (Hazard) leads to the melting of glaciers (Impact)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#contains> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ImpactChainModel> .
